\section*{Nonsingularity and Limit Laws for Random Matrices}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a mathematical result relevant to this question in the selected manuscript. Every fixed regular degree $d\geq3$ is claimed to give GOE eigenvalue statistics at fixed interior bulk energies for uniformly sampled simple regular graphs.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} For fixed \(d\ge3\), let \(G_{n,d}\) be uniform among simple labeled \(d\)-regular graphs, at admissible sizes, and \(\lambda_i\) its adjacency eigenvalues. Fix \(|E|<2\sqrt{d-1}\) and define
\[
 \rho_d(E)=\frac{d\sqrt{4(d-1)-E^2}}{2\pi(d^2-E^2)},\qquad
 \Xi_{n,d,E}=\sum_i\delta_{n\rho_d(E)(\lambda_i-E)}.
\]
For GOE eigenvalues \(\mu_i\), with off-diagonal variance \(1/n\) and diagonal variance \(2/n\), set \(\Xi_n^{\mathrm{GOE}}=\sum_i\delta_{(n/\pi)\mu_i}\). The claim is that each nonnegative continuous compactly supported \(h\) satisfies
\[
 \left|\mathbb E e^{-\int h\,d\Xi_{n,d,E}}
 -\mathbb E e^{-\int h\,d\Xi_n^{\mathrm{GOE}}}\right|\to0.
\]
The random graph has no further conditioning.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
An entropy method gives quantitatively accurate Gaussian eigenvector marks and high moments at sampled edges. Reversible edge switches promote those marks to microscopic orthogonal invariance; a Gaussian perturbation and fixed-energy Dyson relaxation identify the point process, with compact-count control completing convergence.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
At E=0, fixed-energy point-process convergence to a continuous GOE law implies nonsingularity with probability tending to one. This addresses only the random-regular adjacency clause; the bundled permanent and symmetric-determinant distribution questions remain outside. This entry records partial support; complete coverage of the question is not established by this catalogue.

